# ZED Carbon Footprint Management System - Development Rules

## Project Overview
ZED Carbon Footprint is an AI-powered sustainability management platform for Bulgarian SMBs to calculate Scope 1 & 2 carbon emissions, generate reduction strategies, and produce compliance reports aligned with Bulgarian/EU CSRD regulations.

## Technology Stack

### Frontend
- **Framework**: Next.js 14+ with App Router (React 18+)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS with custom green/earth tone palette
- **UI Components**: shadcn/ui components
- **State Management**: React Context API + React Query for server state
- **Charts**: Recharts for data visualization
- **Forms**: React Hook Form + Zod validation
- **Language**: Bulgarian (primary), English (future)

### Backend
- **Runtime**: Node.js with TypeScript
- **Framework**: Next.js API Routes (serverless functions)
- **Database**: Supabase (PostgreSQL) - Local development initially
- **Authentication**: Supabase Auth
- **File Storage**: Supabase Storage
- **OCR**: Google Cloud Vision API (Phase 2)
- **AI/ML**: OpenAI API for strategy generation (Phase 2)

### Database & Security
- **Database**: PostgreSQL via Supabase
- **Row Level Security (RLS)**: Enabled for all tables
- **Authentication**: Supabase Auth with email/password
- **Encryption**: SSL/TLS in transit, AES-256 at rest
- **GDPR**: Full compliance required

## Design Principles

### Visual Design
- **Color Palette**:
  - Primary: Earth green (#2D5016, #4A7729)
  - Secondary: Light green (#8BC34A, #C5E1A5)
  - Accents: Natural brown (#6D4C41)
  - Neutral: White, light gray (#F5F5F5)
  - Alerts: Amber (#FFA726), Red (#E53935)
  - Success: Deep green (#388E3C)
- **Typography**: Sans-serif (Inter or Open Sans), minimum 14px body text
- **Icons**: Lucide React icons, green accents
- **Accessibility**: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance, 4.5:1 contrast ratio

### UI/UX Standards
- Clean, minimalist design with earth tones
- Responsive design (mobile-first approach)
- Bulgarian language interface
- Contextual tooltips throughout ("?" icons)
- Breadcrumb navigation for deep pages
- Loading states for all async operations
- Error handling with user-friendly Bulgarian messages
- Success confirmations with appropriate feedback

### Layout Structure
- Top navigation: Logo, Company Name, User Profile, Notifications, Logout
- Left sidebar: Dashboard, Add Data, Reports, Strategies, Settings, Help
- Main content area: Page-specific content
- Responsive: Collapsible sidebar on mobile (hamburger menu)

## Code Standards

### File Organization
```
app/
├── (auth)/
│   ├── login/
│   └── register/
├── (dashboard)/
│   ├── dashboard/
│   ├── data-entry/
│   ├── reports/
│   ├── strategies/
│   └── settings/
├── api/
│   ├── emissions/
│   ├── strategies/
│   ├── reports/
│   └── calculations/
├── components/
│   ├── ui/ (shadcn components)
│   ├── dashboard/
│   ├── forms/
│   ├── charts/
│   └── layout/
├── lib/
│   ├── supabase/
│   ├── calculations/
│   ├── emissions/
│   └── utils/
└── types/
```

### Naming Conventions
- **Files**: kebab-case (e.g., `emission-calculator.ts`)
- **Components**: PascalCase (e.g., `DashboardCard.tsx`)
- **Functions**: camelCase (e.g., `calculateEmissions`)
- **Types/Interfaces**: PascalCase (e.g., `EmissionData`)
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., `EMISSION_FACTORS`)
- **Database tables**: snake_case (e.g., `emission_data`)

### TypeScript Standards
- **Always use TypeScript** - No JavaScript files
- **Strict mode enabled** - All type checking
- **Type everything** - No `any` types without justification
- **Interfaces over types** for object shapes
- **Enums** for fixed sets of values
- **Zod schemas** for runtime validation

### Component Standards
- **Server Components by default** (Next.js App Router)
- **"use client"** only when necessary (interactivity, hooks, browser APIs)
- **Extract reusable logic** into custom hooks
- **Keep components small** - Single responsibility
- **Props destructuring** in function signature
- **Named exports** for components

### Database Standards
- **RLS policies** on all tables (company_id isolation)
- **Use service role** only in API routes when needed
- **User role access** for frontend queries
- **Proper indexes** on foreign keys and frequently queried columns
- **Timestamps**: created_at, updated_at on all tables
- **Soft deletes**: Use is_active/deleted_at instead of hard deletes

## Bulgarian Language Implementation

### Text Management
- Store all UI text in `lib/i18n/bg.ts`
- Use translation helper functions
- Bulgarian is primary language
- All form labels, buttons, messages in Bulgarian
- Error messages in Bulgarian with clear explanations
- Admin comments and documentation in English

### Bulgarian Terminology
- "Сертификационен орган" (not "Сертификационно тяло")
- "Въглероден отпечатък" for Carbon Footprint
- "Обхват 1" / "Обхват 2" for Scope 1/2
- "tCO2e" (technical term, no translation)
- Follow PRD terminology standards

## Core Feature Requirements

### 1. Authentication & Authorization
- **Roles**: Admin (ZED team), Client (company users)
- **Admin capabilities**: Create companies, manage users, view all data
- **Client capabilities**: Access own company data only
- **Security**: Password complexity, session management, secure password recovery
- **RLS**: Enforce company_id isolation at database level

### 2. Company Master Data
```typescript
interface Company {
  id: string;
  company_name: string;
  registration_number: string;
  industry_sector: string;
  employee_count: number;
  location_count: number;
  primary_contact_email: string;
  billing_address: string;
  logo_url?: string;
  sustainability_goals?: string;
  eu_green_deal_commitment: boolean;
  baseline_year: number;
  created_at: Date;
  updated_at: Date;
}
```

### 3. Emissions Data Collection
- **Scope 1**: Vehicles (fuel type, consumption), On-site fuel, Refrigerants
- **Scope 2**: Electricity (kWh), District heating/cooling
- **Input methods**: Manual forms, Excel/CSV import (MVP), PDF OCR (Phase 2)
- **Validation**: Range checks, period-over-period alerts, mandatory explanations for outliers
- **Multi-location support**: Single location for MVP, multi-location in Phase 2

### 4. Carbon Footprint Calculation Engine
```typescript
// Formula: Total CO2e = Σ(Activity Data × Emission Factor × GWP)
interface EmissionCalculation {
  activity_value: number;
  unit: string;
  emission_factor: number;
  gwp_factor: number; // For refrigerants
  calculated_co2e: number;
}
```
- Bulgarian/EU emission factors (stored in database)
- GHG Protocol Scope 1 & 2 compliant
- Annual emission factor updates
- Calculation transparency (show factors used)

### 5. Dashboard & Visualizations
- **Hero section**: Total footprint, trend indicator, progress to target
- **Action items**: Pending entries, deadlines, recommendations
- **Trend graph**: 12-month line chart (Scope 1 & 2)
- **Breakdown charts**: Donut (Scope 1 vs 2), Bar (by category)
- **Strategy progress**: Active initiatives with progress bars
- Use Recharts with earth-tone color palette

### 6. AI Strategy Generation
- **Analysis**: Identify hotspots, detect inefficiencies, compare to benchmarks
- **Recommendations**: Prioritized by impact (high/medium/low)
- **Categories**: Energy efficiency, renewables, fleet optimization, behavioral changes
- **Tracking**: Planned, In Progress, Completed, Not Applicable
- **Community sharing**: Anonymous success stories

### 7. Reporting System
- **Compliance Reports**: CSRD-aligned, methodology statement, audit trail
- **Internal Reports**: Monthly/quarterly summaries, year-over-year comparisons
- **Stakeholder Reports**: Executive summaries, sustainability certificates
- **Formats**: PDF (primary), Excel, CSV
- **Generation time**: <30 seconds

### 8. Educational Features
- Contextual tooltips throughout ("?" icons)
- Bulgarian/EU regulatory guidance
- First-time user onboarding wizard
- Best practices library
- Plain-language explanations

## API Route Standards

### Structure
```typescript
// app/api/emissions/route.ts
export async function GET(request: Request) {
  try {
    const { searchParams } = new URL(request.url);
    const companyId = searchParams.get('company_id');
    
    // Validate input
    if (!companyId) {
      return NextResponse.json(
        { error: 'Company ID is required' },
        { status: 400 }
      );
    }
    
    // Query with RLS (use user auth)
    const { data, error } = await supabase
      .from('emission_data')
      .select('*')
      .eq('company_id', companyId);
    
    if (error) throw error;
    
    return NextResponse.json({ data });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error:', error);
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: 'Internal server error' },
      { status: 500 }
    );
  }
}
```

### Standards
- **Validate all inputs** using Zod schemas
- **Use RLS** - Prefer user auth context
- **Service role** only when necessary (admin operations)
- **Error handling**: Try-catch with proper HTTP status codes
- **Logging**: Console.error for debugging
- **Return consistent** JSON structure
- **Rate limiting**: Consider for production

## Database Schema Standards

### Core Tables

#### users
```sql
CREATE TABLE users (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  company_id UUID REFERENCES companies(id),
  email TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  first_name TEXT NOT NULL,
  last_name TEXT NOT NULL,
  role TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (role IN ('admin', 'client')),
  is_active BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

#### companies
```sql
CREATE TABLE companies (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  company_name TEXT NOT NULL,
  registration_number TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  industry_sector TEXT NOT NULL,
  employee_count INTEGER,
  location_count INTEGER DEFAULT 1,
  sustainability_goals TEXT,
  eu_green_deal_commitment BOOLEAN DEFAULT false,
  baseline_year INTEGER,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

#### emission_data
```sql
CREATE TABLE emission_data (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  company_id UUID REFERENCES companies(id) NOT NULL,
  location_id UUID REFERENCES locations(id),
  reporting_period DATE NOT NULL,
  scope INTEGER NOT NULL CHECK (scope IN (1, 2)),
  category TEXT NOT NULL,
  activity_value NUMERIC NOT NULL,
  unit TEXT NOT NULL,
  emission_factor NUMERIC NOT NULL,
  calculated_co2e NUMERIC NOT NULL,
  data_source TEXT CHECK (data_source IN ('manual', 'import', 'ocr', 'api')),
  validation_status TEXT DEFAULT 'validated',
  notes TEXT,
  uploaded_by UUID REFERENCES users(id),
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

#### strategies
```sql
CREATE TABLE strategies (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  company_id UUID REFERENCES companies(id) NOT NULL,
  title TEXT NOT NULL,
  description TEXT,
  category TEXT NOT NULL,
  estimated_reduction_co2e NUMERIC,
  status TEXT DEFAULT 'recommended' CHECK (status IN ('recommended', 'planned', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'not_applicable')),
  start_date DATE,
  target_completion_date DATE,
  actual_completion_date DATE,
  actual_reduction_co2e NUMERIC,
  is_shared_community BOOLEAN DEFAULT false,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

#### emission_factors
```sql
CREATE TABLE emission_factors (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  category TEXT NOT NULL,
  subcategory TEXT,
  region TEXT DEFAULT 'Bulgaria',
  value NUMERIC NOT NULL,
  unit TEXT NOT NULL,
  source TEXT,
  effective_date DATE NOT NULL,
  expiry_date DATE,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

### RLS Policies Template
```sql
-- Enable RLS
ALTER TABLE emission_data ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Clients can only see their company's data
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own company data" ON emission_data
  FOR SELECT
  USING (
    company_id IN (
      SELECT company_id FROM users WHERE id = auth.uid()
    )
  );

-- Admins can see all data
CREATE POLICY "Admins can view all data" ON emission_data
  FOR SELECT
  USING (
    EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM users 
      WHERE id = auth.uid() AND role = 'admin'
    )
  );
```

## Calculation Engine Standards

### Emission Calculation Function
```typescript
export function calculateEmissions(params: {
  activityValue: number;
  emissionFactor: number;
  gwpFactor?: number;
}): number {
  const { activityValue, emissionFactor, gwpFactor = 1 } = params;
  
  // Formula: CO2e = Activity × Emission Factor × GWP
  const result = activityValue * emissionFactor * gwpFactor;
  
  // Round to 2 decimal places
  return Math.round(result * 100) / 100;
}
```

### Validation Rules
```typescript
export function validateEmissionData(data: EmissionDataInput): ValidationResult {
  const warnings: string[] = [];
  const errors: string[] = [];
  
  // Range checks
  if (data.activityValue < 0) {
    errors.push('Activity value cannot be negative');
  }
  
  // Period-over-period comparison (if previous data exists)
  if (previousData) {
    const changePercent = Math.abs(
      (data.activityValue - previousData.activityValue) / previousData.activityValue * 100
    );
    
    if (changePercent > 30) {
      warnings.push(`Data differs by ${changePercent.toFixed(1)}% from previous period. Please provide explanation.`);
    }
  }
  
  return { valid: errors.length === 0, warnings, errors };
}
```

## Testing Standards

### Unit Tests
- **Test all calculations** with known inputs/outputs
- **Test validation logic** with edge cases
- **Test API routes** with mock Supabase
- Use Jest + React Testing Library

### Integration Tests
- **Test complete workflows**: Data entry → Calculation → Display
- **Test RLS policies**: Ensure data isolation
- **Test authentication flows**

### Bulgarian Language Testing
- Verify all UI text displays correctly
- Test form validation messages in Bulgarian
- Ensure proper character encoding (UTF-8)

## Performance Standards

### Response Times
- Page load: <2 seconds
- API responses: <1 second
- Report generation: <30 seconds
- Dashboard refresh: <3 seconds

### Optimization
- Use React Server Components for static content
- Implement loading states for async operations
- Lazy load charts and heavy components
- Cache emission factors (Redis future)
- Optimize database queries with proper indexes

## Error Handling

### Frontend
```typescript
try {
  const response = await fetch('/api/emissions');
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch');
  const data = await response.json();
  return data;
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Error fetching emissions:', error);
  toast.error('Възникна грешка при зареждане на данните'); // Bulgarian error
  return null;
}
```

### Backend
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes
- Provide clear error messages
- Log errors with context
- Never expose sensitive information in errors

## Security Checklist

- [ ] All routes protected with authentication
- [ ] RLS policies on all tables
- [ ] Input validation on all forms
- [ ] SQL injection prevention (use parameterized queries)
- [ ] XSS prevention (React escapes by default)
- [ ] CSRF protection (Next.js built-in)
- [ ] Secure password storage (Supabase handles)
- [ ] HTTPS only in production
- [ ] Environment variables for secrets
- [ ] Rate limiting on API routes (future)

## GDPR Compliance

### Data Protection
- **Consent**: User consent for data processing
- **Right to access**: Export user data endpoint
- **Right to erasure**: Soft delete + data anonymization
- **Data portability**: Export in CSV/JSON
- **Breach notification**: Incident response plan
- **Privacy policy**: Bulgarian and English versions

